Installation Steps
==================

Prerequisites
-------------
- Node.js >= 20.0.0 and < 21.0.0 (Node 20.x LTS recommended)
- npm (comes with Node.js)

1. Clone the repository
-----------------------
  git clone <repository-url>
  cd maps-app

2. Install dependencies
-----------------------
  Navigate to the frontend directory and install:

  cd frontend
  npm install

3. Start the development server
--------------------------------
  From the frontend/ directory:

  npm run dev

  The app will be available at http://localhost:5173 (or the port Vite assigns).

4. (Optional) Dev server for phone testing
-------------------------------------------
  Geolocation only works on secure pages. To test on a phone over your LAN:

  npm run dev:phone

  This starts Vite with a self-signed HTTPS certificate accessible on your local network.

5. Run tests
------------
  From the frontend/ directory:

  npm test            # run once
  npm run test:watch  # watch mode

6. Build for production
-----------------------
  From the frontend/ directory:

  npm run build

  This type-checks the project (tsc --noEmit) and then produces a production build in frontend/dist/.
